    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> "Gebruik maximaal één uitgever"@nl, "Use at most one publisher"@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> 1.
_:df_18_33 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#description> "Licentie die van toepassing is op de dataset. Deze licentie wordt overgenomen door alle distributies die geen eigen licentie hebben."@nl, "License applicable to the dataset. This license is inherited by all distributions that do not specify their own license. Publishers MUST make known under which <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/dwbp/#licenses\">license</a> the dataset may be used.\n\nThis license specifies the conditions under which the metadata records in the dataset may be accessed and reused. It does not cover the heritage objects (either physical or digital) that the metadata describes. Access conditions for these objects should be specified in their own descriptions within the dataset.\n\nThe DERA requires metadata to be published openly, so this value SHOULD be an open license that allows consumers to reuse the data, such as `http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/` (CC0), `http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/` (CC BY 4.0), or `http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/` (CC BY-SA 4.0). Adopting a non-open license will severely limit reuse and does not comply with the DERA principles.\n\nThe value MUST be the canonical URI of a license. For example, use `http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/` instead of `http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.nl`."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <https://schema.org/license>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minCount> 1;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#severity> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#Violation>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> "Voeg een licentie toe"@nl, "Add a license"@en.
<https://def.nde.nl/dataset#SchemaLicenseIriProperty> a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#PropertyShape>;
